      "label": "Feathery leaves",
      "description": "Fine, finely divided foliage arranged alternately along slender stems",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Bristly bracts",
      "description": "Prominent hair-like structures beneath the flower heads that give a distinctive bristly appearance",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "Anteaglonium globosum thrives in well-drained, sandy soils of open woodlands and meadows throughout New England, preferring areas with partial shade and consistent moisture.",
